<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: National Toll Roads says '97 trading satisfactory.</title>
<headline>National Toll Roads says '97 trading satisfactory.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Toll Roads Plc said on Tuesday that trading so far in 1997 had been very satisfactory.</p>
<p>The company was currently on budget for the year, chairman Richard Hooper told the annual meeting.</p>
<p>National Toll Roads, which operates the East-Link and West-Link toll bridges over the river Liffey in Dublin, reported a 70.4 percent increase in 1996 pre-tax profit to 5.4 million Irish pounds in March.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
